{"title":"Career Roadmap — Planning Engineer","role":"Planning Engineer","summary":"A Planning Engineer in civil/infrastructure projects is responsible for project scheduling, progress tracking, resource planning, cost/time monitoring, construction coordination, and identifying delays. The role sits at the intersection of civil engineering + project management + construction technology + data analysis.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"Very High — Civil Engineering is one of the strongest undergraduate pathways into planning engineering."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Civil fundamentals, construction methods, surveying, estimation, scheduling and project-planning tools"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Planning Engineer → Senior Planning Engineer; Primavera P6/MS Project, project controls, delay analysis"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Planning Manager / Project Controls Engineer / Project Controls Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Project Controls Director, Planning Head, Program Manager, Construction Technology specialist or independent consultant"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Engineering mathematics, engineering mechanics, basic CAD, programming basics, communication"},{"text":"Understand engineering drawings and basic project quantities"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Structural mechanics, surveying, materials, construction technology, fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Construction-site exposure + quantity estimation"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"RCC/steel basics, transportation, geotechnical engineering, estimation, costing, project management"},{"text":"Primavera P6/MS Project + construction schedule"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Project 